2|0@short^1439990098#cu87aki:MandostheJudge$:There is no true cut-off height. Rather, it's a gliding scale that starts off slowly and becomes more pronounced the shorter a man is. For all intents and purposes it becomes actually noticeable around 5'9/175 cm (speaking for the Netherlands, obviously it varies per country). Around that height you start getting occasional comments about being perceived as short and it's around that height that a not-insignificant number of women (around 20% or so) will exclude you from the dating pool right of the bat because of your height. The 'height malus' then increases the shorter a man is, slowly at first but picking up speed for every inch a man 'lacks'. 
