-1|0@short^1439961522#cu7yje0:iamelroberto$:Could it be that your circle of influence is providing some confirmation bias as this point? Not accusing you of spending a bit too much time in this sub but maybe tomorrow try asking a random short person how oppressed they feel because of their height. Be honest with yourself about what their answer means. Could be that they have a very extreme perspective. Could be one that agrees with yours. Could not. What I think you're saying is that short people are being oppressed with or without their knowledge. But what I'm not sure you understand is that people's realities are in a large part made up of their own belief systems. If I believe that all fat people hate me, I'm gonna only notice the fat people who are sneering at me. That's evidence based psychology right there. I'm wondering if maybe your perspective is highly reinforced by others in this sub. What worries me is that we are both looking at the same world full of some nice people and some ignorant. Whereas I'm seeing the nice ones you may only be seeing the ignorant. And whereas I know ignorant ones exist I'm not sure that you really know many nice ones too. Obviously all people are not prejudice ignorant people not are they all nice and open minded to people who have (insert anything here) difference. But I want you to know it's important to keep in our minds that there are both and people in between the two. And your "problem" is really no better or worse than anyone else's. But it's yours so own it don't complain and make it other people's fault. There tends to be an ideal body in various cultures. We all seem to vary in SOME way from that ideal and we are ALL insecure about that difference. But fuck that dude. That different is what makes us US. Are you fucking kidding me? I'm 5'4 and I love it. I wouldn't be another height if you offered. You need to own it for everyone else who is different from the ideal (which is everyone). You show them that this is your difference (likely one of several) and relate to them about theirs. They make act like they don't have one. They do. And they know it intimately. Use this as a resource to help you relate with others. Not to blame (and thus separate) yourself from others. Ok thanks (takes breath). 
3|0@short^1439963797#cu7zesr:Ser_devon_black$:&gt; e) difference. But I want you to know it's important to keep in our minds that there are both and people in between the two. And your "problem" is really no better or worse than anyone else's. But it's yours so own it don't complain and make it other people's fault. There tends to be an ideal body in various cultures. We all seem to vary in SOME way from that ideal and we are ALL insecure about that difference. But fuck that dude. That different is what makes us US. Are you fucking kidding me? I'm 5'4 and I love it. I wouldn't be another height if you offered. You need to own it for everyone else who is different from the ideal (which is everyone). You show them that this is your difference (likely one of several) and relate to them about theirs. They make act like they don't have one. They do. And they know it intimately. Use this as a resource to help you relate with others. Not to blame (and thus separate) yourself from others. Ok thanks (takes breath). I understand what you are sying and I think your message of focusing on the positive is a good one. Life is too short to only fight battles and we should relax and enjoy the things we take for granted from time to time. However I also don't think we should only bury our heads in the sand and ingore the fact that the problem of heightism is increasing in a scary rate. Note that this is a forum for venting and the only place where we aren't attacked and ridiculed (as much as other places) for doing such so the focus might be more on the negative side since it's good to vent. Heightism isn't the only factor but it's a major factor that goes together with others, if you are for instance a little short but very very good looking you might be a good loking guy, if you are slightly short and average or even a little ugly you are the short ugly "manlet" etc. I think many factors take place in other peoples judgement and tehy need to overall be taken into account for "the scale" to tip over to hostile or good. But the thing is, heightism and demands on height ahve been so blown out of proportions in some cultures, and the whole concept of height is so hard to determine. It's not liek being overweight wich is quite obvious to the eye and also a health issue. Wheat exactly is short? most people have no idea of what the average is and have a false perception due to media and memes. Many people feel a societal pressure and also girls feel peer pressure forcing them to take other peoples viewpoints regarding the potential mates height into consideration. Also add the fact that height is so packed with stigmas making it an extremely hard topic to discuss without being ridiculed. If you are short and try to live life confidently and say fuck it "I am great" you get accused of having napoleon complex, if you claim heightism you get dismissed and laughed at, and if they take you seriously they claim that fat people, women and black people have it much worse and you should just suck it up. Again, I think culture plays a huge role, I lived in Sweden and for me to find postive people was a lot harder then when I was in the US. Now that I live in Japan the only people giving me shit for my height are other Northern Europeans so it's a lot easier to cope, tho I still recognize the problem and take interest in it. I however absolutely think it's important that we as short men don't knock other short men down for having problems that we don't, we need to be accepting of the fact that some people may have it worse or better. 
1|0@short^1439993024#cu88rq8:iamelroberto$:If you felt like I was trying to knock anyone down or invalidate their experience I'm sorry that was not my intention. I get that it's very frustrating for some people to be short particularly if you have nothing else going for you. And maybe being tall with all else being the same would be considered better by society. But so would ANY talent or skill. Why are we not focusing on what we can change instead of what we can't. When we complain we're literally just demonstrating to everyone else how NOT to help themselves make a better life. You referred to me not noticing the "oppression" as burying my head in the sand. But could it be possible that you too have your head in the sand? Maybe you are ignoring all of the times when people are actually more concerned with themselves and their own faults than yours. You come across as being very attached to this story of oppression and even if you think it only leaks out while venting in this sub it does not. It infects everything you do and how you perceive the actions of others. You're also supporting to create that reality for others who are perfectly happy interacting with others currently, who will now worry "did they just say that because I'm short?" Do you honestly believe that you've improved this persons life? Or anyone's? I don't agree that this sub is only for venting, I believe positive stories and comments about being short are as important if not much more so. Negative stories, comments and venting make other people feel bad about themselves, and I don't see how that has or will lead to anything good. It will not make "heightism" go away to point these things out. You know what will? Invalidating heightism by not giving it any credibility. Social prejudice is not the same as legal prejudice. Legal prejudice can be changed by fighting. I don't know how social prejudice can be fixed but I don't see that this is the way and is causing damage in the mean time. My concern 